{
 "source": "Every usage type in a rule's \"match\" list, and every \"miss\" that names the same offer, is a usageType value copied from the AWS Price List bulk API: https://pricing.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/offers/v1.0/aws/<offer>/current/us-east-1/index.csv, the offer named in each entry, fetched 2026-11-12. A \"miss\" is a nearby real usage type (or the same one under another service) that the rule must not match.",
 "serviceNames": "Service names are the ServiceName values of the official FOCUS 1.0 sample (test/fixtures/focus/official-sample.csv) where it has the service, otherwise the Price List serviceName. Cost Explorer SERVICE values differ in places (for example \"Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud - Compute\"), which is why the service gates in candidates.js match a fragment without case.",
 "notCovered": "ElasticIP:IdleAddress (the idle-ip rule) is kept from the first release but is not in the current Price List; PublicIPv4:IdleAddress is.",
